  "brief": "Sanofi is acquiring Insmed for $41 billion, its largest pharma deal in nearly three years, to expand its respiratory and rare disease portfolio.\n\nSanofi / Insmed (Announced): Sanofi to Acquire Insmed. Sanofi is acquiring Insmed for $41 billion in the biggest pharma deal in nearly three years [1, 2, 3]. The deal will expand Sanofi's respiratory and rare disease portfolio [5, 7]. Insmed will be acquired by Sanofi in cash for $175 per share [6]. The acquisition was announced by Sanofi [4, 8].\nCrowdStrike / Zscaler (Announced): CrowdStrike and Zscaler Deal. CrowdStrike and Zscaler are merging in an all-stock deal worth $43.9 billion [16, 11, 10]. The deal will create a cybersecurity giant, according to the CEO of CrowdStrike [12, 16, 11]. The acquisition is expected to be completed with a share exchange ratio of 1.135 [17, 16, 11].\nAmazon / Decart (Announced): Amazon Acquires Decart. Amazon is acquiring Decart, an Israeli AI startup, to narrow the gap with Nvidia in AI chip technology [24, 25, 26]. The deal is reportedly worth $7.5 billion [25, 26, 28]. The acquisition was announced by Amazon [24, 28].\nLinamar / Genie (Announced): Linamar and Genie Deal. Linamar Corporation is acquiring Genie from Terex Corporation [33, 34, 35]. The deal was announced by Linamar Corporation [32, 33]. The acquisition significantly expands Linamar's Access Work Platforms Group [34, 35].\nBlackstone, Warburg Pincus, Apollo / Global Payments (Rumored): Blackstone, Warburg Pincus, Apollo Back Global Payments. Blackstone, Warburg Pincus, Apollo in talks to back GTCR's $50 billion Global Payments deal [36, 37]. The deal is rumored to be backed by these investors [36, 37]. No further information is available at this time [36, 37].\nClariant / Ashland (Rumored): Clariant and Ashland in Talks. Clariant and Ashland are in talks to acquire Ashland [38, 39, 40]. The deal is reportedly worth around $3.39 billion [40, 41]. The stage of the deal is currently rumored [38, 39, 40].\nFamily Savings / CUTimes (Announced): Family Savings and CUTimes Deal. Family Savings is acquiring CUTimes [45, 46]. The deal was announced [45]. Nothing new is reported [46].\nTownsquare Media / Mackinac Island ferries owner (Announced): Townsquare Media Rejects Mackinac Island Ferries Bid. Townsquare Media has rejected a takeover bid from the owner of Mackinac Island ferries [47, 48, 49]. The company's board has also rejected a $2.03-per-share takeover bid [48]. The bid was reportedly worth $37 million [47, 49].",
